{"number":2,"title":"Whole Numbers","slug":"whole-numbers","color":"","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Class 6 IMO — Whole Numbers: the number line, properties (closure, commutative, associative, distributive), patterns, and simplifying expressions with brackets.","topics":[{"title":"Whole Numbers & Their Properties","concept":"<p><strong>Whole numbers</strong> are 0, 1, 2, 3, … The smallest whole number is 0 and there is no largest. Natural numbers start from 1.</p><p>Key properties: addition and multiplication are <strong>commutative</strong> (a + b = b + a) and <strong>associative</strong>, and multiplication is <strong>distributive</strong> over addition: a × (b + c) = a × b + a × c.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Which property does 7 + 5 = 5 + 7 show?","solution":"The commutative property of addition."},{"number":"2","problem":"Use the distributive property: 4 × (10 + 2).","solution":"4 × 10 + 4 × 2 = 40 + 8 = 48."}],"recap":["Whole numbers: 0, 1, 2, 3, … (smallest is 0).","Commutative: a + b = b + a; distributive: a × (b + c) = a×b + a×c."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is the smallest whole number?","options":["0","1","−1","10"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The smallest whole number is 0.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Using the distributive property, 6 × (5 + 2) = ?","options":["32","42","13","40"],"correct":1,"explanation":"6 × 5 + 6 × 2 = 30 + 12 = 42.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"The Number Line & Successor/Predecessor","concept":"<p>Whole numbers can be shown on a <strong>number line</strong>. Moving right adds and moving left subtracts. The <strong>successor</strong> of a number is one more; the <strong>predecessor</strong> is one less.</p><p>0 is the only whole number with no predecessor (in whole numbers).</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"What is the successor of 99?","solution":"99 + 1 = 100."},{"number":"2","problem":"On a number line, where does 3 + 4 land?","solution":"Start at 3 and move 4 right to reach 7."}],"recap":["Successor = number + 1; predecessor = number − 1.","0 has no predecessor among whole numbers."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is the predecessor of 1000?","options":["1001","999","990","100"],"correct":1,"explanation":"1000 − 1 = 999.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Which whole number has no predecessor?","options":["0","1","10","100"],"correct":0,"explanation":"0 is the smallest whole number, so it has no predecessor.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"Patterns, Brackets & Simplifying","concept":"<p>When simplifying, do the work inside <strong>brackets first</strong>, then multiplication and division, then addition and subtraction (the BODMAS order).</p><p>So 2 + 3 × 4 = 2 + 12 = 14, and 12 − (3 + 4) = 12 − 7 = 5.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Simplify 12 − (3 + 4).","solution":"Brackets first: 12 − 7 = 5."},{"number":"2","problem":"Simplify 2 + 3 × 4.","solution":"Multiply first: 2 + 12 = 14."}],"recap":["Do brackets first, then × and ÷, then + and −.","This order is called BODMAS."],"quiz":[{"q":"Simplify: 20 − (5 × 2) = ?","options":["10","30","20","15"],"correct":0,"explanation":"5 × 2 = 10, so 20 − 10 = 10.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Simplify: (8 + 2) × 3 = ?","options":["14","24","30","26"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Brackets first: 10 × 3 = 30.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":18,"questions":[{"q":"Which property does 3 × 4 = 4 × 3 show?","options":["commutative","associative","distributive","closure"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Changing the order without changing the result is the commutative property.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Continue the pattern:  1, 3, 5, 7, ___ ?","options":["8","9","10","11"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Odd numbers go up by 2: 7 + 2 = 9.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Using the distributive property, 5 × (20 + 1) = ?","options":["100","105","101","120"],"correct":1,"explanation":"5 × 20 + 5 × 1 = 100 + 5 = 105.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"The smallest whole number is ___ ?","options":["0","1","−1","2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The smallest whole number is 0.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is the successor of 999?","options":["998","1000","990","1001"],"correct":1,"explanation":"999 + 1 = 1000.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Simplify: 7 × (10 + 5) = ?","options":["75","105","85","120"],"correct":1,"explanation":"7 × 15 = 105.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Simplify: 36 − (6 × 4) = ?","options":["12","24","30","8"],"correct":0,"explanation":"6 × 4 = 24, so 36 − 24 = 12.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Simplify: (15 + 5) ÷ 4 = ?","options":["4","5","6","20"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Brackets first: 20 ÷ 4 = 5.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Simplify: 8 + 2 × 5 = ?","options":["18","50","20","16"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Multiply first: 8 + 10 = 18.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Simplify: 100 − (40 + 30) = ?","options":["30","70","130","10"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Brackets first: 100 − 70 = 30.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A box holds 5 + 5 = 10 pens. How many pens in 12 such boxes?","options":["110","120","130","100"],"correct":1,"explanation":"12 × 10 = 120 pens.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A worker earns ₹500 each day. How much in 6 days?","options":["₹2,500","₹3,000","₹3,500","₹2,000"],"correct":1,"explanation":"500 × 6 = ₹3,000.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Simplify: 3 + 4 × (10 − 2) ÷ 8 = ?","options":["5","7","8","9"],"correct":1,"explanation":"10 − 2 = 8, then 4 × 8 ÷ 8 = 4, so 3 + 4 = 7.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"Use the distributive property: 17 × 8 + 17 × 2 = ?","options":["150","160","170","180"],"correct":2,"explanation":"17 × (8 + 2) = 17 × 10 = 170.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"}]}}}